@startuml FreefallUseCaseDiagram

left to right direction

actor User
actor "Physics Researcher" as Researcher
actor "Educator" as Educator
actor "Student" as Student
actor "External System" as External

rectangle "Freefall Simulation System" {
  usecase "Configure Simulation" as UC1
  usecase "Run Simulation" as UC2
  usecase "Visualize Results" as UC3
  usecase "Export Data" as UC4
  usecase "Analyze Results" as UC5
  usecase "Calculate Trajectory" as UC6
  usecase "Update Physics" as UC7
  usecase "Manage Energy Calculations" as UC8
  usecase "Configure Air Resistance" as UC9
  usecase "Set Initial Conditions" as UC10
  usecase "Handle Collisions" as UC11
  usecase "Validate Physics" as UC12
  usecase "Compare Integration Methods" as UC13
  usecase "Adjust Simulation Speed" as UC14
  usecase "Configure Visualization" as UC15
  usecase "Run Educational Scenario" as UC16
  usecase "Export Simulation State" as UC17
  usecase "Import Configuration" as UC18
}

User --> UC1
User --> UC2
User --> UC3
User --> UC4
User --> UC14
User --> UC15
Researcher --> UC5
Researcher --> UC12
Researcher --> UC13
Educator --> UC3
Educator --> UC5
Educator --> UC16
Student --> UC2
Student --> UC3
Student --> UC16
External --> UC4
External --> UC17
External --> UC18

UC1 .> UC10 : includes
UC1 .> UC9 : includes
UC1 .> UC14 : includes
UC1 .> UC15 : includes
UC2 .> UC6 : includes
UC6 .> UC7 : includes
UC6 .> UC8 : includes
UC6 .> UC11 : includes
UC2 .> UC3 : includes
UC2 .> UC4 : extends
UC5 .> UC3 : includes
UC5 .> UC4 : includes
UC13 .> UC2 : includes
UC16 .> UC1 : includes
UC16 .> UC2 : includes
UC16 .> UC3 : includes

note top of UC1
  Configuration includes:
  - Initial height
  - Initial velocity
  - Gravity value
  - Time step
  - Air resistance settings
  - Apple properties
  - Integration method
  - Simulation speed
  - Visualization options
end note

note right of UC8
  Energy calculations include:
  - Potential energy (mgh)
  - Kinetic energy (½mv²)
  - Total mechanical energy
  - Energy conservation verification
  - Energy vs time graphs
end note

note left of UC13
  Integration method comparison:
  - Euler method
  - Verlet integration
  - Runge-Kutta method
  - Accuracy analysis
  - Performance benchmarking
  - Error quantification
end note

note bottom of UC16
  Educational scenarios:
  - Basic freefall demonstration
  - Energy conservation lesson
  - Air resistance effects
  - Gravity variation experiments
  - Numerical methods comparison
end note

@enduml
